# ── Internal working documents ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repo is PUBLIC (the -private suffix is historical). Internal material —
# dev plans, handoffs, audits, review packets — belongs in cli-pulse-internal,
# per the partner handover doc. These patterns keep a stray `git add -A` from
# publishing the untracked working set at the repo root permanently.
# Root-anchored so docs/ content is unaffected. Already-tracked files are
# unaffected by gitignore (e.g. historical DEV_PLAN/PROJECT_FIX commits stay).
/HANDOFF_*.md
/CODEX_*.md
/PROJECT_REVIEW*.md
/ART_ASSET_LIST*.md
/CLI_PULSE_ACTION_CHECKLIST*.md
/PLAN_*.md
/PROJECT_PLAN_*.md
/PROJECT_AUDIT_*.md
/PUBLIC_EXPOSURE_*.md
/PUBLIC_REPO_*.md
/R0_OWNER_*.md
/REPO_VISIBILITY_STRATEGY.md
/RELEASE_WORKFLOW.md

# The same document names, at ANY depth — deliberately not root-anchored.
#
# The list above was written on 2026-07-31 with the note "root-anchored so
# docs/ content is unaffected". On 2026-08-07 a single `git add -A` staged 141
# internal documents and pushed them here (PR #421, closed): 91 at the root and
# 50 that root-anchoring could never have caught — 49 under `docs/` and
# `MachineRootHelper/SHIP_RUNBOOK.md`. The anchoring was the hole, and
# `PROJECT_FIX_*` — the single largest class, and the one the habit still
# produces — had no entry at all.
#
# These mirror LAYER 1 of scripts/check_no_internal_docs.sh so the two agree.
# The gate catches what reaches the index; these keep it out of the index in
# the first place. Only the gate matches case-insensitively on purpose: these
# patterns inherit `core.ignorecase`, which is true on this macOS checkout
# (so `postmortem_x.md` is caught here) and false on a case-sensitive
# filesystem (where it is not). The gate is the layer that holds either way —
# do not let these lull anyone into treating it as redundant.
#
# Nothing tracked matches (verify: `git ls-files | grep -iE 'PROJECT_FIX|...'`
# returns nothing, which is also what the gate asserts on every CI run).
*PROJECT_FIX*
*DEV_PLAN*
*DEVELOPMENT_PLAN*
*FIX_PLAN*
*SESSION_CHECKPOINT*
*SHIP_CHECKLIST*
*POSTMORTEM*
*POST_MORTEM*
*RUNBOOK*

# ── iCloud Drive collision copies ──────────────────────────────────────────
# This working tree lives in iCloud Drive, which resolves a same-name conflict
# by silently writing a second file with " 2" (then " 3", …) appended — to any
# name: sources, SQL migrations, whole directories. 21 of them rode along in
# the 2026-08-07 `git add -A`, including `scripts/check_no_internal_docs 2.sh`
# and duplicate `migrate_v0.72_provider_accounts` files. A duplicate migration
# is the worst case: migrations are matched BY NUMBER and are the only record
# of what has run against production, so a second `v0.72` turns "did v0.72
# run?" into "which v0.72?" — see the migration-numbering rule in AGENTS.md.
#
# Masks nothing legitimate: `git ls-files | grep -E ' [2-9](\..*)?$'` is empty.
# If a real file ever needs a name like `Figure 2.png`, `git add` refuses it
# out loud ("paths are ignored by one of your .gitignore files") rather than
# dropping it silently, and `git add -f` is the deliberate override.
* [2-9]
* [2-9].*

# ── Local-only developer tooling (deliberately untracked) ──────────────────
# Real files that belong on this machine and nowhere else. Listing them here
# is what keeps `git status` honest: an untracked file nobody intends to commit
# is indistinguishable from one somebody forgot to.
#
# xcode_devid_fan_embed.sh — a Developer-ID fan-embed build phase wired into
#   the Xcode target by an uncommitted pbxproj edit; it mirrors step 4b of the
#   tracked scripts/build_signed_app.sh and is useless without that local edit.
# *_tmp.* — scratch prompts for AI review runs. They quote internal DEV_PLANs
#   verbatim while carrying none of the names the gate greps for, so they are
#   exactly the kind of file that slips past every other layer here.
# submit_v1_10_7.py — a one-off App Store submission script from 2026-04,
#   superseded by the tracked submit_v1_10_8.py / submit_v1_11_0.py. Ignored
#   rather than deleted because it is nobody's duplicate; safe to delete.
/scripts/dev/xcode_devid_fan_embed.sh
/scripts/dev/*_tmp.*
/CLI Pulse Bar/scripts/submit_v1_10_7.py
